 transformed reciprocal function of the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{a}{bx+c}+d\n$$\n\nhas the horizontal asymptote $y=d,$ and therefore, its range is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,d)\\cup (d,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $d=\\frac{2}{3}.$ Therefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=\\frac{2}{3},$ and the range of the function is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,\\frac{2}{3})\\cup (\\frac{2}{3},\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe graph $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929417/assets/c218be8082733d6e1026b8d6f810d43ba4ea3e10928f43260a34a1c4cde7f7f6.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243289 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66d82fa3-d576-5c42-9dca-4e1b76473424" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76cb2f54-28c5-5369-8213-e80862043177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243291} {:answer/id #uuid "6a644b12-14e3-5c6a-ae68-30b97d1c185e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a644b12-14e3-5c6a-ae68-30b97d1c185e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243292} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd57aaa5-32fc-5c6a-bc7f-9b38f23d3388" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243290} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbd71a96-70f3-5cd1-9a94-2c43357a0878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbd71a96-70f3-5cd1-9a94-2c43357a0878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243294} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9f66283-f5ba-5a40-8bb4-35130c337f8c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :a